---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import FAQ from '../components/FAQ.astro';
import { faqSchema } from '../lib/schema';
import { abs } from '../lib/utils';

const gaming = [
  { q: 'What are the best gaming tips for beginners?', a: 'Learn the basics of one game at a time, keep one sensitivity and control layout long enough to build muscle memory, practice in short focused sessions, and review your mistakes instead of only counting wins. Good habits like warming up and taking breaks matter more than any single trick.' },
  { q: 'How can I improve my aim in FPS games?', a: 'Pick one sensitivity you can keep, place your crosshair at head height before enemies appear, and practice a short routine of tracking and flicking each day. Fix your setup first (mouse surface, monitor refresh rate, stable frame rate), because inconsistent hardware makes aim feel inconsistent.' },
  { q: 'How do I increase FPS on my PC?', a: 'Update your graphics driver, close background apps, then lower the settings that cost the most performance, usually shadows, volumetric effects, ray tracing and resolution scaling. Check temperatures too: a hot CPU or GPU slows itself down, and no setting can fix that.' },
  { q: 'What causes input lag and how do I reduce it?', a: 'Input lag is the delay between pressing a button and seeing the result on screen. It comes from your input device, the game and GPU pipeline, and your display. Raising frame rate, using a wired or low-latency connection, enabling a game’s low-latency mode and using a fast display all help.' },
  { q: 'What is the best sensitivity for gaming?', a: 'There is no universal best. Choose a sensitivity that lets you turn around comfortably with a natural arm movement and still make small corrections precisely. Many players land in a middle range and then adjust slowly. Change it rarely so your muscle memory can settle.' },
  { q: 'Is PC or console better for gaming?', a: 'Neither is better for everyone. Consoles offer simplicity, a fixed target for developers and a lower upfront cost. PCs offer more upgrade paths, settings control and input options. Pick based on the games you play, your budget and whether you enjoy tuning hardware.' },
  { q: 'Is a high refresh rate monitor worth it?', a: 'For fast games, yes, if your system can actually produce frames to match. A 144 Hz or faster display looks smoother and reduces perceived blur, but a game running at 60 FPS will not benefit. Check what frame rate your PC reaches in the games you play before paying extra.' },
  { q: 'How do I fix game lag?', a: 'First work out whether it is low FPS (stutter or choppy visuals) or high ping (delayed actions online). For ping, use a wired connection and check for background downloads. For FPS, lower demanding settings and check temperatures. Our troubleshooting guide walks through both step by step.' },
];
const site = [
  { q: 'Does DistritoGamer earn money from the links on this site?', a: 'It may. We can earn a commission when you buy through certain links, at no extra cost to you. We may also show advertising. Commissions never decide what we recommend, and affiliate links appear only where a product is relevant to the guide.' },
  { q: 'Do you test the products you write about?', a: 'Only when we say so. Where a guide discusses a type of gear without hands-on testing, it says that plainly and focuses on what to look for and who each type suits. We do not invent reviews, ratings, prices or specifications.' },
  { q: 'How often are guides updated?', a: 'Evergreen guides are reviewed every 6 to 12 months and game-specific guides after major patches. The updated date on a guide changes only when we make a substantive revision.' },
  { q: 'Can I suggest a guide or report a mistake?', a: 'Yes. Use the contact page to tell us which guide, what is wrong and, if possible, a source. We correct verified errors promptly. Guide suggestions are welcome too, especially for games or problems you could not find a good answer to.' },
];
const all = [...gaming, ...site];
const schema = [faqSchema(all)];
---
<PageLayout title="Gaming FAQ: Quick Answers to Common Questions" heading="Frequently asked questions" description="Quick, direct answers to common gaming questions about aim, FPS, input lag, sensitivity, PC vs console, plus how DistritoGamer works." path="/faq/" schema={schema} updated="2026-10-06"
  intro="Short answers to the questions players ask most, with links to the full guides." wide>
  <div style="max-width:var(--read)">
    <FAQ items={gaming} heading="Gaming questions" id="gaming" />
    <p>Want the long version? Start with our <a href="/gaming-tips/">gaming tips guides</a>, <a href="/game-settings/">game settings guides</a> and <a href="/gaming-performance/">gaming performance guides</a>, or search the site for anything specific.</p>
    <FAQ items={site} heading="About DistritoGamer" id="site" />
    <p>More detail is in our <a href="/editorial-policy/">editorial policy</a> and <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">affiliate disclosure</a>. Still stuck? <a href="/contact/">Contact us</a>.</p>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
